# Clinic Management System: Modules, Roles and Access Specification

Stack: Node.js + Express, MySQL, React + Ant Design.
Status key used throughout: **[V1]** already built in the delivered code, **[V1+]** partly built, **[NEW]** to be built.

---

## 1. Purpose and scope

A single web system that follows a patient from the front desk to discharge and keeps the money, stock, staff and audit trail behind it. Everything is role-based: a user only sees the screens and actions their role allows, and every sensitive action is written to the audit log.

### 1.1 Patient journey (who touches the patient, in order)

| Step | Where | Role | System action |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Reception / Cashier | Receptionist, Cashier | Register or find patient, pay card or consultation fee, get queue number |
| 2 | Triage | Nurse | Record vitals, chief complaint, triage priority |
| 3 | OPD room | Doctor | Consultation, diagnosis, orders (lab, imaging, drugs, procedures) |
| 4 | Cashier | Cashier | Pay for ordered services (or credit/insurance approval) |
| 5 | Laboratory / Imaging | Lab tech, Imaging tech | Collect sample or perform scan, enter result or report |
| 6 | Doctor | Doctor | Review results, finalise treatment |
| 7 | Pharmacy | Pharmacist | Dispense paid prescription, stock reduces |
| 8 | Ward (if admitted) | Doctor, Ward nurse | Admission, bed, rounds, medication chart, discharge |
| 9 | Finance | Accountant | Daily cash reconciliation, receivables, expenses, reports |

---

## 2. Roles

| Code | Role | Main job in the system |
|---|---|---|
| ADM | System administrator | Users, roles, settings, master data, backups. No clinical or financial entry by default |
| MGR | Medical director / Manager | Read all dashboards and reports, approve high-value actions |
| REC | Receptionist / Registration clerk | Patient registration, appointments, queue |
| CSH | Cashier | Collect payments, issue receipts, refunds (with approval), shift closing |
| NUR | Triage / OPD nurse | Vitals, triage, OPD nursing notes, injections and dressings |
| DOC | Doctor | Consultation, orders, prescriptions, admission, discharge |
| WRD | Ward nurse | Inpatient nursing care, medication administration, bed management |
| LAB | Laboratory technician | Sample handling, test results, lab stock requests |
| IMG | Imaging technician / Radiologist | X-ray, ultrasound and other scans, image reports |
| PHA | Pharmacist | Dispense, drug stock in dispensary, drug returns |
| STO | Store keeper | Main store, receiving, issuing, stock counts, purchase requests |
| ACC | Accountant / Finance officer | Ledgers, expenses, receivables, payables, financial reports |
| HRO | HR officer | Staff records, attendance, leave, payroll, contracts |
| AUD | Auditor | Read-only access to finance, stock and the audit log |

A user can hold more than one role (for example, a small clinic where one person is both cashier and receptionist). Permissions are the union of all assigned roles.

