### 4.3 Triage and vitals [V1+]

**Purpose:** capture measurements and priority before the doctor sees the patient.

**Functions**
- Vitals: blood pressure, temperature, pulse, respiratory rate, SpO₂, weight, height, BMI (auto), MUAC for children, blood glucose (optional). [V1]
- Chief complaint and triage category (emergency, urgent, routine). [V1+]
- Early-warning score and out-of-range highlighting (for example SpO₂ below 92). [NEW]
- Pregnancy status and last menstrual period for women of reproductive age. [NEW]
- Growth chart data for under-5s. [NEW]
- Reorder queue by triage priority. [NEW]
- Nursing procedures from OPD: injection, dressing, nebulisation, observation, charged to the bill. [NEW]

**Access**

| Role | Access |
|---|---|
| NUR | Create and edit vitals for open visits (edit window configurable, for example 24 hours) |
| DOC | Read; may add or correct vitals during consultation (logged) |
| WRD | Create vitals for inpatients |
| MGR, AUD | Read |

**Permissions:** `vitals.create`, `vitals.read`, `vitals.update`, `triage.set`, `nursing.procedure.create`.

