### 4.4 OPD, outpatient consultation [V1]

**Purpose:** the doctor's workspace for one visit.

**Functions**
- Visit created from appointment, queue or walk-in. [V1]
- History, examination, diagnosis (free text now, ICD-10 coded later), plan, follow-up date. [V1, ICD-10 NEW]
- Orders: lab tests, imaging, prescriptions, procedures, referral, admission. [V1 lab and prescriptions]
- Previous visits, lab results, allergies and active medications visible in the visit screen. [V1+]
- Prescription templates and drug interaction / allergy warning. [NEW]
- Sick leave note, medical certificate, referral letter, with clinic letterhead and print. [NEW]
- Close visit: needs diagnosis; closed visits are locked. Reopen needs a reason (doctor in charge or manager). [V1, reopen NEW]
- Follow-up and recall list. [NEW]
- Doctor's own patient list and day summary. [NEW]

**Access**

| Role | Access |
|---|---|
| DOC | Full on own consultations; read all patient history; cannot edit another doctor's closed notes |
| NUR | Vitals and nursing notes only |
| LAB, IMG, PHA | Read only the orders addressed to them and the minimum patient details |
| MGR | Read |
| AUD | Read; every read of a full record is logged |

**Permissions:** `visit.create`, `visit.read`, `visit.update`, `visit.close`, `visit.reopen`, `order.lab.create`, `order.imaging.create`, `prescription.create`, `referral.create`, `certificate.create`, `diagnosis.create`.

**Break-glass:** a doctor opening a patient they have no visit with must enter a reason. The access is flagged in the audit log.

