### 4.15 Audit log [NEW]

**Purpose:** prove who did what, when, from where, and what changed.

**What is logged**

| Category | Events |
|---|---|
| Authentication | Login success and failure, logout, password change and reset, lockout, two-factor events |
| Users and roles | User created, edited, deactivated, role or permission changed |
| Patient data | Patient created, edited, merged; **record opened** (read access), break-glass access, print and export |
| Clinical | Visit created, edited, closed, reopened; orders, results entered, amended, released; prescriptions |
| Money | Invoice created, voided; payment, refund, discount, waiver; shift opened and closed; journal posted and reversed; period closed |
| Stock | Item created, price changed, GRN, issue, transfer, adjustment, write-off, count approved |
| HR | Staff edited, contract change, salary change, leave approval, payroll approved, payslip viewed |
| System | Settings changed, backup and restore, data import and export, failed API authorisation |

**Record structure**

```
audit_logs
  id, occurred_at (UTC), user_id, user_name, role_at_time,
  action            e.g. billing.payment.create
  entity_type, entity_id
  patient_id        (when relevant, for per-patient access reports)
  before_json, after_json   (changed fields only)
  reason            (required for void, refund, amend, reopen, break-glass)
  ip_address, user_agent, session_id, branch_id
  prev_hash, row_hash        (hash chain to detect tampering)
```

**Rules**
- Append-only: the application database user has insert and select rights on this table, never update or delete.
- Hash chain: each row stores a hash of the previous row, and a nightly job verifies the chain and alerts on a break.
- Retention: keep at least the period your local health-records and tax rules require (commonly 7 to 10 years); archive older rows rather than deleting.
- Sensitive values (passwords, tokens, full card numbers) are never written to the log.

**Screens:** filter by user, action, entity, patient, date and IP; "who viewed this patient" panel; per-record history tab; export; saved alerts (for example, more than five failed logins, refund above limit, access outside working hours).

**Access:** AUD full read and export; ADM and MGR read; nobody can edit or delete. Reading the audit log is itself logged.

**Permissions:** `audit.read`, `audit.export`, `audit.alert.manage`.

