## 12. Default seed roles and the first-day checklist

1. Create the 14 roles in section 2 with their permissions from sections 4 and 7.
2. Create the first administrator and force a password change at first login.
3. Load master data: departments, wards and beds, service price list, lab and imaging catalogues, formulary, suppliers, chart of accounts.
4. HR enters staff; admin creates their users and assigns roles.
5. Set approval limits (section 6.4), receipt and MRN formats, clinic letterhead.
6. Run a day of test patients through the full journey (section 8.1), then check the cashier shift, stock cards and audit log all agree.
7. Turn off demo users, confirm backups run, go live.